{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068636-the-soul-shaped","id":1068636,"title":"The Soul-Shaped","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-27T06:22:16-07:00","id":1068636,"title":"The Soul-Shaped","content":"So, this is based on a Mystery I though up (and may have posted elsewhere). Basically these are Sleepwalkers (and even Sleepers, if you want) who have essentially had their souls shaped like a Legacy does.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, they are part of a Legacy (either an existing one, or a custom one just for these).<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Pick a thematic (for the Legacy) Skill for the Primary and another Skill for the Secondary Arcana associated with the Legacy. These skills are treated as if they were Arcana rating for the purposes of dice pool, Reach, Attainments, etc.</li> <li>Treat their Willpower as their Gnosis rating when needed.</li> <li>They can either store up to 5 Mana (which they get via Legacy Oblations only), or can spend Willpower in place of Mana (and the Legacy Oblations are another Willpower source).</li> </ol>This gives characters (NPC, or PC, if desired) a small but potent set of powers, in a familiar rules construct. The Legacy Attainment nature of their powers means you don't have to worry about the effects of dispelling, Paradox, or Dissonance. Of course the easier acquisition of Skill dots, and Willpower starting out higher (and being slightly cheaper to increase) means they will be higher powered than an equivalent XP Mage. Albeit limited only to their Attainments.<br /> <br /> As to <i>how</i> a person could get their soul shaped in such a manner, well, that was the Mystery.<br /> <hr /><br /> <u><b>Examples:</b></u><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Let's take an &quot;average&quot; person and the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1052518#post1052518\">Tamers of Fire</a>.</li> <li>Since it seems to be about using the concept of fire as inspiration, let's use Expression for Mind, and Persuasion for Forces.</li> <li>They'll have a Willpower of 4 (2 Resolve, 2 Composure), and a 2 in Expression and Persuasion.</li> <li>This means they will have the first Attainment and its secondary function (effectively Mind 2, Forces 2, Gnosis 4), but they won't have the second Attainment in this case because it also requires Athletics 3 (and we are assuming they only have 2s).</li> </ol><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-30-2017, 11:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T13:01:27-07:00","id":1068814,"title":"","content":"This sounds like a possible replacement for Proximi, a stronger one that doesn't suffer under Paradox or Dissonance. It would have the potential, depending on how rare it is, to greatly enhance the place of non Mages in the Orders.<br /> Two things I would do different:<br /> \u200b1-Taking the Sleepwalker Merit is part of the cost, either separately or the cost is added into the price of gaining this Template.<br /> \u200b2-They don't hold stored Mana, their Attainments are fueled by Willpower points and those points can only be recovered the way any mortal does it; Vice, Virtue or rest. This way they don't overpower the actual Mages but can still pump out the magic when needed, but not frivolously. Rest alone would give them one point a day to spend, beyond that most times they would lean heavily on their Vice, encouraging all sorts of positive behavior like alcoholism and other addictions.<br /> <br /> \u200bPersonally I would make this something Mages know how to do, just not easily with great cost and consumption of time and unlike Proximi this trait wouldn't be passed on through genetics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T13:34:13-07:00","id":1068840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068636-the-soul-shaped?p=1068814#post1068814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like a possible replacement for Proximi, a stronger one that doesn't suffer under Paradox or Dissonance. It would have the potential, depending on how rare it is, to greatly enhance the place of non Mages in the Orders.<br /> Two things I would do different:<br /> \u200b1-Taking the Sleepwalker Merit is part of the cost, either separately or the cost is added into the price of gaining this Template.<br /> \u200b2-They don't hold stored Mana, their Attainments are fueled by Willpower points and those points can only be recovered the way any mortal does it; Vice, Virtue or rest. This way they don't overpower the actual Mages but can still pump out the magic when needed, but not frivolously. Rest alone would give them one point a day to spend, beyond that most times they would lean heavily on their Vice, encouraging all sorts of positive behavior like alcoholism and other addictions.<br /> <br /> \u200bPersonally I would make this something Mages know how to do, just not easily with great cost and consumption of time and unlike Proximi this trait wouldn't be passed on through genetics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, Proximi have more flexibility than Shaped would, being able to configure factors and Reach, and having access to more distinct spells. These gain in depth (being able to reach Adept and Master level effects) what they lack in breadth (they have, at most, 10 distinct effects).<br /> <br /> These aren't intended as a replace of anything. I just was working through thought experiments, and these are nice and simple, mechanically. Few changes compared to an already existing system. Light-weight (mechanically, at least).<br /> <br /> Still, I'd hope some other Mage games might find a use for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T23:05:51-07:00","id":1069139,"title":"","content":"They wouldn't actually replace the Proximi, since the families can exist without the interference of Mages, but within the Orders themselves I could see the Shaped taking on important roles, especially if the Mages are somehow responsible for choosing them to gain their splat.<br /> \u200bThe families, passing their gifts down the bloodline, would continue to be treasured by Mages for their long term benefits. Eugenics anyone?<br /> \u200bThe Shaped would work better with Sleepers and especially if they can be crafted would be picked for specific roles within society. They would assume the role of skilled professionals.<br /> \u200bI like this idea and I'm wondering if I could work it into the idea that Sleepwalkers can carry spells. Perhaps requiring a five or six dot Mage and permanently releasing the spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 03-28-2017, 02:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T08:42:34-07:00","id":1070675,"title":"","content":"I like it better as, at its core, a Mystery rather than another tool in the Mage toolbox. That's not to say the Shaped wouldn't or shouldn't be used. Particularly if they're Sleepwalkers they'd serve as great aids and are potentially more accessible than Proximi. I think allowing them to be Sleepers would be more interesting. With the Shaped not invoking Paradox with the ability because of it being a Legacy attainment it could work well. Many (most) of them are probably Sleepwalkers, though. <br /> <br /> For the Mystery, like the idea of this being some powerful entity in the area. Maybe a Gulmoth that intruded because of a Paradox and now goes around reshaping people's souls to &quot;fit&quot; the shape of the one that brought it to the Fallen World. Cutting pieces away, maybe even adding pieces on, until it's <i>reasonably</i> close to the Legacy. This lets the individual access the attainments but causes a fair bit of damage (derangement) during the process and maybe even ongoing. It picks targets through some strange set of criteria. This could create an interesting dilemma for those who unravel this Mystery. It's Abyssal and it's mutilating souls. But the Shaped can be just so damn useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7892-malraza","name":"Malraza","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T08:56:12-07:00","id":1070681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malraza</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1068636-the-soul-shaped?p=1070675#post1070675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it better as, at its core, a Mystery rather than another tool in the Mage toolbox. That's not to say the Shaped wouldn't or shouldn't be used. Particularly if they're Sleepwalkers they'd serve as great aids and are potentially more accessible than Proximi. I think allowing them to be Sleepers would be more interesting. With the Shaped not invoking Paradox with the ability because of it being a Legacy attainment it could work well. Many (most) of them are probably Sleepwalkers, though.<br /> <br /> For the Mystery, like the idea of this being some powerful entity in the area. Maybe a Gulmoth that intruded because of a Paradox and now goes around reshaping people's souls to &quot;fit&quot; the shape of the one that brought it to the Fallen World. Cutting pieces away, maybe even adding pieces on, until it's <i>reasonably</i> close to the Legacy. This lets the individual access the attainments but causes a fair bit of damage (derangement) during the process and maybe even ongoing. It picks targets through some strange set of criteria. This could create an interesting dilemma for those who unravel this Mystery. It's Abyssal and it's mutilating souls. But the Shaped can be just so damn useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. It was originally a plot hook - Non-Mages shouldn't even be able to have Legacies, so how is this possible. But I thought it might be worth sharing on its own since it is so mechanically simple - just slap a Legacy on a person, subbing Skill for Arcana and Willpower for Gnosis. It's not even all that hard to justify how everything fits together Lore-wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}